course: dictionary
lesson: 1261
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer chose. «The burr stuck to my sock after the walk.» Socks and walks are the clues, so burr here is a prickly seed case.
explain: «The metal had a rough burr where it was cut.» Metal and cut are the clues, so this burr is a rough edge left after cutting. It is the same word, but the clues show a different meaning.
explain: «He had a soft burr in his voice.» Here burr means a way of speaking with a rolled r sound. Swap each meaning into the sentence and check which one still makes sense.
fact: A burr is a prickly seed case that sticks to clothes or fur.
fact: «Burrs» means more than one burr, and burrs often hook onto fur, which helps seeds travel.
fact: A burr can also be a rough edge left on metal or wood after cutting.
fact: A burr can be a rolled r sound in some accents, such as Scottish or West Country speech.
fact: Burdock burrs are covered in tiny hooks; George de Mestral looked at them under a microscope and invented Velcro in the 1940s.
exercise: «Some seeds hook onto animals' fur, like burdock burrs.» What is a burr in this sentence? | A soft voice with a rolled r | *A prickly seed case | A rough edge on metal | A kind of bird
exercise: «The metal had a rough burr where it was cut.» What does burr mean here? | *A rough edge left after cutting | A prickly seed case | A type of parachute | A rolled r sound
exercise: «Burrs are seed heads covered in tiny hooks.» Which word tells you that burrs grow on plants? | *seed | covered | hooks | tiny
test: «He had a soft burr in his voice.» What does burr mean here? | A tiny hook | A prickly seed case | *A rolled r sound in an accent | A rough edge on wood
test: «Children pick burrs off their socks after a walk.» What does burr mean here? | A sharp metal tool | *A prickly seed case | A rolled r sound | A piece of bread
exam: In «The burr stuck to my sock after the walk», which clues show that burr means a seed case? | The voice and the accent | The wood and the paint | The metal and the cut | *The sock and the walk
